Embedded React: fork a repaint across workers by area, once per commit.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/core/er_parallel.c,
engine/core/renderer_internal.h and engine/scene/compositor.c.

Each damage rect of at least 16 rows per worker forked across every worker on
its own, so a row of cards repainting as six rects woke eight threads six times
and walked the tree 48 times, and a narrow focus ring forked as wide as the
screen. A damage-clipped commit now forks once for all its rects: worker k
renders each rect's rows in its band, the bands cut so that each holds about an
equal share of the damaged area, at least 16 rows and ER_SLICE_MIN_PIXELS
(128 Ki) each. A full repaint slices by the same minimum. Workers without a
band are not woken. Output is unchanged: bands clip like the serial passes.

